Package: linux-tutor
Version: @VERSION@
Section: education
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Linux Tutor maintainers <linux-tutor@localhost>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-pyqt6 | python3-pyside6.qtwidgets, python3-pyte, python3-yaml, python3-markdown, podman (>= 4.0), uidmap, util-linux
Recommends: passt | slirp4netns, fuse-overlayfs, fonts-dejavu-core
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Homepage: https://example.invalid/linux-tutor
Description: interactive, hands-on Linux learning and assessment environment
 Linux Tutor teaches Linux from first steps to system administration in the
 spirit of the classic DOS tutors: structured lessons and lectures, a genuine
 Bash shell running in an isolated rootless Podman laboratory, practical
 exercises marked on their outcome (any valid method is accepted), progressive
 hints, end-of-lesson assessments and level examinations, progress tracking
 and an ungraded practice mode.
